    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm putting together a doc for our new CI/CD pipeline. Can you give me a quick breakdown of the standard stages—specifically Code Commit, Automated Testing, Staging, and Production—and what kind of quality gates we should have at each step?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your CI/CD pipeline, the **Code Commit** stage requires linting and static analysis to ensure code quality early on. **Automated Testing** should incorporate unit, integration, and potentially performance tests with a high pass rate gate. Before **Staging**, thorough end-to-end testing and security scans (e.g., vulnerability checks) are crucial for a functional environment. Finally, **Production** deployment requires final approval gates, monitoring setup, and often a canary release strategy before full rollout.",
      "source": "target",
