    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That looks solid. Could you expand a bit more on the \"Automated Testing\" and \"Staging\" gates specifically? I want to make sure we have enough safeguards in place so that nothing unexpected or problematic slips through those gates into production.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In **Automated Testing**, your primary gates should enforce critical bug-free status, often requiring 90%+ unit test coverage and 100% passing integration tests before progression. For **Staging**, focus on environment parity checks to ensure the staging mirrors production dependencies and data structure. Beyond functional testing, implementing user acceptance testing (UAT) sign-offs and load testing within staging prevents performance bottlenecks or unexpected user experience failures.",
      "source": "target",
